# WAYFINDER environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in values. `.env.local` is git-ignored.
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. WAYFINDER runs fully without any of them:
# the aviation-data providers are public and need no credential, and the AI
# layer degrades to a deterministic, source-grounded explanation when unset.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI explanation and translation layer (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint. The key is read only on the
# server (src/lib/ai/llm.ts) and is never sent to the browser. If the key is
# absent, /api/announcement returns aiGenerated:false with an explicit
# "not configured" explanation instead of failing.
#
# Check the provider's current pricing and availability before enabling this.
# A free signup does not guarantee a free API tier.
# WAYFINDER_AI_API_KEY=
# WAYFINDER_AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# WAYFINDER_AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web-search discovery (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google-powered discovery uses grounding with Google Search on the Gemini API.
# This is the supported path for a NEW implementation: the older Custom Search
# JSON API is closed to new customers and is scheduled for discontinuation on
# January 1, 2027, and the Site Restricted JSON API ceased serving traffic on
# January 8, 2025. Grounding with Google Search returns the pages Google found, as
# structured groundingChunks, which is exactly what discovery needs.
#
# The key is read only on the server (src/lib/assist/providers/discovery.ts) and
# is never sent to the browser.
#
# COST AND AVAILABILITY — check the current figures before enabling:
#   Grounding with Google Search is a PAID feature; there is no free tier for the
#   tool itself. As documented on the Gemini API pricing page:
#     - Gemini 3.x models: 5,000 free search requests per month (shared across
#       all Gemini 3.x models), then $14 per 1,000 requests.
#     - Gemini 2.5 models: up to 1,500 grounded prompts/day free on the paid
#       tier (500/day on the free tier), then $35 per 1,000 grounded prompts.
#   Model availability, prices and limits change; verify them at
#   https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing before enabling.
#
# When the key is absent the discovery provider is skipped with an explicit
# "missing credentials" reason and the curated official-source directory is used
# instead. Nothing else breaks.
#
# A key that is present but not permitted to run the paid Search-grounding tool
# (billing not enabled, free-tier-only project, quota exhausted) fails with a
# 4xx. That failure is classified and surfaced on the page as a discovery
# limitation — it is never reported to the traveller as "no source covers this
# place". Enable billing on the Google Cloud project before relying on discovery.
# WAYFINDER_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# WAYFINDER_GOOGLE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# WAYFINDER_GOOGLE_SEARCH_MODEL=
